<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <!--
        Packing line work center.

        The operation is packing: tissue packs go in, cartons come out. One work
        center is enough - there is no rewinding or log-sawing to model.

        noupdate="1" is deliberate: costs_hour is tuned by the accountant against
        real payroll and power bills, and a module upgrade must not overwrite that
        with the placeholder below.

        THE HOURLY COST IS A PLACEHOLDER. Replace it before go-live. It should
        carry labour + electricity + a share of machine depreciation, so a
        manufacturing order's cost reflects real packing cost rather than
        materials wearing a disguise.

        Work centers, operations and work orders are all present in Odoo 18
        Community. What is NOT present is mrp_workorder, the Enterprise Shop Floor
        tablet interface - operators record work orders from the standard backend
        list view. Confirmed absent from the odoo:18.0 image.

        ================================================================
        TWO FIELDS ARE NOT SET HERE AND MUST BE SET IN THE UI
        ================================================================

        Both are on Manufacturing > Configuration > Work Centers > Packing Line.
        Neither can be written from this file, and both matter.

        1. EXPENSE ACCOUNT  ->  503900 Conversion Cost Absorbed

        This is the single highest-value field in the Phase 2 setup. When a
        manufacturing order is marked done, mrp_account's _post_labour picks the
        credit account like this:

            account = wo.workcenter_id.expense_account_id
                      or product_accounts['expense']

        Left blank, the fallback is the finished product's expense account -
        501200 COGS - Manufactured Goods. Absorbed conversion cost would then be
        credited straight INTO manufacturing COGS, netting against it, while the
        actual packing wages sit in 601100 next to the office payroll. Result:
        manufacturing margin reads better than it is, and the trading-versus-
        manufacturing comparison this whole chart exists to produce is quietly
        wrong in the direction that flatters the factory.

        Pointed at 503900, the credit lands beside 503100-503400 (the actual
        factory costs) under Cost of Revenue, and the difference between them is
        the under/over-absorption variance - which is what tells you whether
        costs_hour is anywhere near reality.

        Not settable here: Odoo 18 generates account XML IDs per company, so
        ref() to an account is not portable. Same reason somgreen_config carries
        no account references at all - see its manifest.

        2. ANALYTIC DISTRIBUTION  ->  Production (Cost Centre plan)

        Creating the analytic account routes nothing to it. mrp_account's
        _create_or_update_analytic_entry_for_record only creates analytic lines
        when the work center itself carries an analytic_distribution:

            if self.workcenter_id.analytic_distribution or ...

        Not settable here either: analytic_distribution is a JSON field keyed by
        analytic account database id, which is not known at data-load time.
    -->

    <record id="workcenter_packing" model="mrp.workcenter">
        <field name="name">Packing Line</field>
        <field name="code">WC-PCK</field>
        <field name="costs_hour">12.00</field>
        <field name="time_efficiency">100</field>
        <field name="default_capacity">1</field>
        <field name="time_start">10</field>
        <field name="time_stop">10</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
